 "_note": "The linking standard on D'Arcy, adopted 18 October 2026. THE PATTERN WIDTH IS 'LOCATORS + NAMED SOURCES': a passage is a citation when it quotes an archive reference (a National Archives, Gloucestershire, Trove, Queensland, NAA, ITM/DR or local-register locator) or names a record set (FamilySearch, FreeREG, FreeBMD, FindMyPast, Discovery, the Internet Archive...). It is NOT event wording (baptised, buried, married, died, census, will, deed: those patterns were measured and left out, 363 passages against these 144) and the census and register reference tables count only where a row quotes a locator or a named source. record_links.hosts is empty on purpose: the gate cannot tell a front door (a search form) from a record, so only the archive's own entries and the links its Rec component marks (data-cite) count, and a Rec is written only where the address carries the record's own reference. Exemptions are the attributes data-cite-exempt / data-name-exempt on the page, each with its reason; EX is ratcheted in .standardfloor.json.",
